      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "DBI versions before 1.651 for Perl do not enforce statement handle consistency with the row.  When the statement handle had no fields but the source row was non-empty, the internal row-buffer helper would read from a negative array index.  This could be triggered by a caller supplying inconsistent metadata and rows to the prepare method.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
